  "title": "October 10 Weekly Observation — NVIDIA's Throne Maintenance and the Eastern Semiconductor Chill",
  "summary": "As NVIDIA maintains the Sun's position at $5.55T market cap, simultaneous decline of East Asian semiconductor planets has been observed.",
  "body": "<h3>Stability of the Sun</h3><p>During this week's observation period, NVIDIA maintained the Universe's Throne with a market cap of $5.55T. Its stable dominance from the same position as last week suggests the firmness of the highest power seat. The order of the top 5 planets—Apple ($4.88T), Alphabet ($4.29T), Microsoft ($3.97T), Amazon ($2.82T)—remained unchanged.</p><h3>Stark Contrast Between Rise and Fall</h3><p>In weekly gains, Walmart (+6.7%) traced the steepest ascent curve, followed by Amazon (+3.9%) and Tesla (+3.6%). These appear to have gained positive momentum in consumer goods and technology sectors. Conversely, the East Asian semiconductor sector showed concentrated decline. SK Hynix (-8.2%), Samsung Electronics (-4.8%), and TSMC (-4.6%) recorded simultaneous losses, indicating the region's gravitational pull in the universe is weakening.</p><h3>Subtle Orbital Fluctuations</h3><p>In the universe's admission system, Visa achieved new entry into the upper ranks, while ASML departed from its previous position. Planets with high potential for future promotion being tracked include Advantest and Fortinet, with Dell (momentum 250), Seagate Technology (247), and MediaTek (236) drawing gradual upward trajectories within strong ascending currents.</p><h3>Recorded Order</h3><p>The second week of October 2026 recorded two simultaneous signals: continuity of existing dominance and simultaneous weakness of eastern semiconductors. The universe turns, and this observation remains.</p><div class=\"col-chart\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 310\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"wg2\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"0\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#9c7a3a\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#f2ba3c\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"700\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#10141f\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#f2ba3c\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"800\">This Week's Stars — Ignited Stars and Cooling Stars</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"56\" fill=\"#8a94b8\" font-size=\"12.5\" font-weight=\"600\">Earth TOP 20 Weekly Market Cap Change — Gainers and Losers</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"95\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Walmart</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"80\" width=\"310\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"url(#wg2)\"/><text x=\"520\" y=\"95\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">+6.7%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"128\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Amazon</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"113\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"url(#wg2)\"/><text x=\"391\" y=\"128\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">+3.9%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"161\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Tesla</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"146\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"url(#wg2)\"/><text x=\"377\" y=\"161\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">+3.6%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">SK Hynix</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"178\" width=\"380\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#386ee1\"/><text x=\"590\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">-8.2%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Samsung Electronics</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"211\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#386ee1\"/><text x=\"432\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">-4.8%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"259\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">TSMC</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"244\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#386ee1\"/><text x=\"423\" y=\"259\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">-4.6%</text><text x=\"674\" y=\"296\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#9c7a3a\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"800\">UNIVERTRIX · univertrix.com</text></svg></div><div class=\"col-chart\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 300\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"wg\" x1=